{"run_id": "20260830T111332-free-sql-168561", "qid": "gabriel-gf-03", "repeat": 0, "system": "free-sql", "config_hash": "4cc587a8ef30", "git_sha": "b0a569a-dirty", "question": "Which analyses use the HistFitter framework for their statistical analysis?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analyses that use the HistFitter framework for their statistical analysis are 2006.05880, 2011.07812, 2102.01444, 2106.01676, and 2211.08028. Each explicitly states that likelihood fits are performed in HistFitter (e.g., 2006.05880: \"profile likelihood fit … implemented in the HistFitter framework\"; 2011.07812: \"The HistFitter package is used for statistical interpretation\"; 2102.01444: fits use \"HistFitter and pyhf\"; 2106.01676: \"profile log-likelihood fit … implemented in the HistFitter framework\"; 2211.08028: \"profile likelihood fit … implemented in the HistFitter framework\"). Paper 2401.05299 was not included because its statistical-method entity and text do not mention HistFitter.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2006.05880", "2011.07812", "2102.01444", "2106.01676", "2211.08028"], "value": null, "steps": [{"tool": "search", "round": 1, "args": {"text": "HistFitter framework"}, "rows": 20, "error": null, "preview": "entity_id | kind | label\nhepkg:method:histfitter | statistical_method | HistFitter statistical framework\nhepkg:method:profile-likelihood-fit-histfitter | statistical_method | HistFitter fit\nhepkg:meth"}, {"tool": "sql", "round": 1, "args": {"query": "SELECT kind, COUNT(*) FROM entity WHERE lower(label) LIKE '%histfit%' GROUP BY kind"}, "rows": 1, "error": null, "truncated": false, "preview": "kind | COUNT(*)\nstatistical_method | 3\n(1 rows)"}, {"tool": "sql", "round": 2, "args": {"query": "SELECT a.paper_id, a.assertion_id, a.subject_id, a.object_id, e.label FROM assertion a JOIN entity e ON e.entity_id = a.object_id WHERE a.predicate='result_uses_statistical_method' AND (a.object_id IN ('hepkg:method:histfitter','hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-fit-histfitter','hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-fit') OR lower(e.label) LIKE '%histfit%')"}, "rows": 7, "error": null, "truncated": false, "preview": "paper_id | assertion_id | subject_id | object_id | label\n2006.05880 | hepkg:assertion:c3d98c05b03ead8abe0724ae | hepkg:result:d5288b5bc0407b0b2005d131 | hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-fit | Maximum-l"}, {"tool": "sql", "round": 2, "args": {"query": "SELECT paper_id, entity_id, kind, label FROM entity_occurrence WHERE entity_id IN ('hepkg:method:histfitter','hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-fit-histfitter','hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-fit') OR lower(label) LIKE '%histfit%'"}, "rows": 7, "error": null, "truncated": false, "preview": "paper_id | entity_id | kind | label\n2006.05880 | hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-fit | statistical_method | Profile likelihood fit implemented in HistFitter\n2006.05880 | hepkg:method:histfitter | stat"}, {"tool": "sql", "round": 3, "args": {"query": "SELECT entity_id, canonical_id, cluster_size FROM entity_canonical WHERE entity_id IN ('hepkg:method:histfitter','hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-fit-histfitter','hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-fit','hepkg:method:pyhf-combination')"}, "rows": 1, "error": null, "truncated": false, "preview": "entity_id | canonical_id | cluster_size\nhepkg:method:profile-likelihood-fit | hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-fit | 3\n(1 rows)"}, {"tool": "sql", "round": 3, "args": {"query": "SELECT DISTINCT s.paper_id, eo.label FROM evidence s JOIN entity_occurrence eo ON eo.paper_id = s.paper_id WHERE lower(s.quote) LIKE '%histfitter%' AND eo.entity_id IN ('hepkg:method:histfitter','hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-fit-histfitter','hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-fit')"}, "rows": 0, "error": "no such column: s.paper_id", "truncated": false, "preview": "ERROR: no such column: s.paper_id"}, {"tool": "sql", "round": 4, "args": {"query": "SELECT e.bundle_id, p.arxiv_id, e.quote FROM evidence e JOIN paper p O